('reading', 'short_answer', 'Marine Biology', 'medium', 6, 'Name one physical or biological item that might be found in a ballast tank''s water, according to the passage.', '21000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002', null, null, '["fish larvae","planktonic crustaceans","algae","bacteria","eggs","cysts","microscopic eggs and cysts of marine species"]', 'The passage lists "fish larvae, planktonic crustaceans, algae, bacteria, and the microscopic eggs and cysts of numerous marine species" as contents of ballast tanks.', 'Any single item from the list given in paragraph 2 is an acceptable answer for this type of open short-answer question.', '{"short_answer"}', 45, 12, false),
('reading', 'true_false_not_given', 'Marine Biology', 'hard', 7, 'Researchers agree that biofouling is now a more significant pathway for species introduction than ballast water.', '21000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002', null, null, '"NOT GIVEN"', 'The passage says biofouling "may now rival ballast water," which is a tentative, hedged claim from "some studies," not a statement that researchers agree it is now more significant.', 'The word "may" and the qualifier "some studies suggest" show this is not a settled consensus, so a claim of clear researcher agreement goes beyond the text.', '{"true_false_not_given"}', 65, 13, false),
('reading', 'short_answer', 'Psychology', 'medium', 6, 'Who is credited with the formal introduction of cognitive load theory in the 1980s?', '21000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000003', null, null, '["John Sweller","Sweller"]', 'The passage states the theory was introduced "by the educational psychologist John Sweller in the 1980s."', 'Names of key researchers are usually given in the first sentence introducing a theory, making this an easy early-question target.', '{"short_answer"}', 40, 1, false),
('reading', 'true_false_not_given', 'Psychology', 'medium', 6, 'Long-term memory has a strictly limited storage capacity, similar to working memory.', '21000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000003', null, null, '"FALSE"', 'The passage describes long-term memory as "an effectively unlimited store," which contradicts the claim that it has a strictly limited capacity like working memory.', 'The contrast between "limited" working memory and "effectively unlimited" long-term memory is explicit in the same sentence — read both halves before answering.', '{"true_false_not_given"}', 55, 2, false),
('reading', 'matching_information', 'Psychology', 'hard', 7, 'Which paragraph explains the three distinct sources of cognitive load identified by researchers?', '21000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000003', null, '["Paragraph 1","Paragraph 2","Paragraph 3","Paragraph 4","Paragraph 5"]', '"Paragraph 2"', 'Paragraph 2 defines intrinsic, extraneous, and germane load as "three distinct sources of this cognitive demand, or load."', 'Look for the paragraph containing all three named types of load together, rather than one that discusses only a single type.', '{"matching_information"}', 70, 3, false),
('reading', 'matching_features', 'Psychology', 'hard', 7, 'Match each description to the correct type of cognitive load: Arises from the inherent difficulty of the material itself, regardless of how it is taught.', '21000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000003', null, '["Intrinsic load","Extraneous load","Germane load"]', '"Intrinsic load"', 'The passage states "Intrinsic load arises from the inherent complexity of the material itself," matching this description exactly.', 'The phrase "regardless of how it is taught" is a strong clue, since only intrinsic load is described as independent of instructional presentation.', '{"matching_features"}', 60, 4, false),
('reading', 'matching_features', 'Psychology', 'hard', 7, 'Match each description to the correct type of cognitive load: Considered the primary target for improvement through better instructional design.', '21000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000003', null, '["Intrinsic load","Extraneous load","Germane load"]', '"Extraneous load"', 'The passage states extraneous load "is considered the primary target for improvement through better instructional design, since it represents cognitive effort that contributes nothing to learning."', 'Only extraneous load is described as a target for design improvement, distinguishing it from intrinsic (fixed by content) and germane (desirable) load.', '{"matching_features"}', 60, 5, false),
('reading', 'matching_features', 'Psychology', 'hard', 7, 'Match each description to the correct type of cognitive load: Represents productive mental effort devoted to integrating new information into existing knowledge.', '21000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000003', null, '["Intrinsic load","Extraneous load","Germane load"]', '"Germane load"', 'The passage defines germane load as "the mental effort genuinely devoted to processing and integrating new information into existing knowledge structures," describing it as generally desirable.', 'Germane load is the only one of the three explicitly labelled "generally considered desirable," which distinguishes it clearly from extraneous load.', '{"matching_features"}', 60, 6, false),
('reading', 'sentence_completion', 'Psychology', 'medium', 6.5, 'Complete the sentence using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS: The "split-attention effect" occurs when learners must mentally integrate information sources that are physically or ______ separated.', '21000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000003', null, null, '"temporally"', 'The passage states the split-attention effect occurs when sources of information "are physically or temporally separated."', 'The blank sits between two similar-sounding qualifiers ("physically" and the missing word) joined by "or" — expect a word of the same grammatical type.', '{"sentence_completion"}', 55, 7, false),
('reading', 'multiple_choice', 'Psychology', 'medium', 6.5, 'According to the passage, why can presenting identical text and narration simultaneously impair learning?', '21000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000003', null, '["Because learners generally prefer one format over the other","Because reconciling the two redundant channels occupies working memory needed for comprehension","Because narration is always slower than reading text silently","Because most learners cannot read fluently while listening"]', '"Because reconciling the two redundant channels occupies working memory needed for comprehension"', 'The passage explains that "attempting to reconcile identical text and speech occupies working memory capacity that would otherwise be available for genuine comprehension."', 'The explanation for the redundancy effect is given directly after the term is introduced — read the sentence that follows the definition.', '{"multiple_choice"}', 70, 8, false),
('reading', 'true_false_not_given', 'Psychology', 'medium', 6.5, 'Studies have found that novice learners generally benefit more from studying worked examples than from unguided problem-solving.', '21000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000003', null, null, '"TRUE"', 'The passage states studies "have repeatedly found that studying worked examples produces superior learning outcomes... compared with attempting to solve equivalent problems from scratch" for novices.', 'This is a direct restatement of the "worked example effect" described in the passage; confirm the group referenced (novices) matches.', '{"true_false_not_given"}', 55, 9, false),
('reading', 'true_false_not_given', 'Psychology', 'hard', 7, 'The worked example effect provides the same degree of benefit for learners at every level of expertise.', '21000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000003', null, null, '"FALSE"', 'The passage states this advantage "does not hold indefinitely as learners gain expertise" and describes the "expertise reversal effect," directly contradicting equal benefit at every level.', 'A claim of benefit "at every level" should be checked against any mention of a reversal or exception further in the same paragraph or the next one.', '{"true_false_not_given"}', 65, 10, false),
('reading', 'short_answer', 'Psychology', 'hard', 7, 'What term describes the finding that instructional techniques helpful to novices can become counterproductive for more experienced learners?', '21000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000003', null, null, '["the expertise reversal effect","expertise reversal effect"]', 'The passage names this "the ''expertise reversal effect,'' whereby instructional techniques that benefit novices... become progressively less helpful and can even become counterproductive."', 'The term appears in quotation marks immediately before its definition, a common pattern for locating short-answer terminology questions.', '{"short_answer"}', 55, 11, false),
('reading', 'true_false_not_given', 'Psychology', 'hard', 7, 'Cognitive load theory''s critics dispute the validity of its core experimental findings.', '21000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000003', null, null, '"FALSE"', 'The passage states critics, "while generally not disputing its core experimental findings," instead question whether the principles translate to real classrooms — the opposite of disputing the core findings.', 'Watch for a concessive clause like "while generally not disputing X" — it tells you the following criticism is about something else (application), not X itself.', '{"true_false_not_given"}', 65, 12, false),
('reading', 'short_answer', 'Psychology', 'medium', 6.5, 'According to the passage, what do most studies rely on to measure cognitive load, in the absence of direct physiological measurement?', '21000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000003', null, null, '["self-reported effort ratings or performance outcomes","indirect proxies such as self-reported effort ratings or performance outcomes"]', 'The passage states most studies rely "on indirect proxies such as self-reported effort ratings or performance outcomes rather than any direct physiological measurement."', 'The phrase "rather than" signals the contrast between what is actually used (the answer) and what is not used (physiological measurement).', '{"short_answer"}', 55, 13, false),
('reading', 'short_answer', 'Urban Planning', 'easy', 5.5, 'Who is credited with articulating the modern concept of the fifteen-minute city?', '21000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000004', null, null, '["Carlos Moreno"]', 'The passage states the concept was "first articulated in its modern form by the scientist and urbanist Carlos Moreno."', 'Names attached to a concept typically appear in the first sentence that introduces that concept.', '{"short_answer"}', 40, 1, false),
('reading', 'true_false_not_given', 'Urban Planning', 'medium', 6, 'The idea of a self-sufficient neighbourhood was first proposed in the twenty-first century.', '21000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000004', null, null, '"FALSE"', 'The passage states "urban theorists throughout the twentieth century repeatedly proposed variations on the notion of self-sufficient neighbourhoods," meaning the idea predates the twenty-first century.', 'Note the distinction between when the underlying idea originated (twentieth century) and when its current specific form was articulated (recently) — the question asks about the former.', '{"true_false_not_given"}', 55, 2, false),
('reading', 'true_false_not_given', 'Urban Planning', 'medium', 6, 'Paris and Melbourne have both adopted versions of the fifteen-minute city concept in their planning strategies.', '21000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000004', null, null, '"TRUE"', 'The passage states "Several cities, including Paris and Melbourne, have adopted variations of the concept as explicit components of their long-term planning strategy."', 'Both named cities are given in the same sentence, so a single scan confirms the answer for both at once.', '{"true_false_not_given"}', 45, 3, false),
('reading', 'multiple_choice', 'Urban Planning', 'medium', 6.5, 'According to the passage, why do many twentieth-century suburbs pose a challenge for implementing the fifteen-minute city?', '21000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000004', null, '["They were built with no roads suitable for cycling","They were designed assuming widespread private car ownership, spreading housing and services apart","They have too high a population density for local amenities","Local governments there refuse to consider any planning changes"]', '"They were designed assuming widespread private car ownership, spreading housing and services apart"', 'The passage states such cities "grew rapidly... around the assumption of widespread private car ownership, resulting in low-density suburbs where housing, employment, and services are often kilometres apart by design."', 'Eliminate options describing high density or lack of roads, since the passage specifically describes these suburbs as low-density and car-dependent by design.', '{"multiple_choice"}', 65, 4, false),
('reading', 'sentence_completion', 'Urban Planning', 'medium', 6, 'Complete the sentence using NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS: Retrofitting existing suburbs often requires relaxing zoning restrictions to permit small shops, clinics, and ______ within residential areas.', '21000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000004', null, null, '"workspaces"', 'The passage lists "small shops, clinics, and workspaces within residential areas" as things zoning changes would permit.', 'This is a straightforward list-completion task; locate the three-item list and select the final item as the missing word.', '{"sentence_completion"}', 50, 5, false),
('reading', 'true_false_not_given', 'Urban Planning', 'hard', 7, 'Critics argue that fifteen-minute city policies could worsen inequality between wealthy and poorer neighbourhoods.', '21000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000004', null, null, '"TRUE"', 'The passage states "the fifteen-minute city risks exacerbating existing inequalities," describing how wealthier neighbourhoods may improve while poorer ones "may be left further behind."', '"Exacerbating existing inequalities" is the key paraphrase for "worsen inequality" in the question.', '{"true_false_not_given"}', 55, 6, false),
('reading', 'true_false_not_given', 'Urban Planning', 'hard', 7.5, 'City officials involved in fifteen-minute city projects have proposed restricting how far residents may travel.', '21000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000004', null, null, '"FALSE"', 'The passage explicitly states "no city implementing the concept has proposed restricting residents from travelling wherever they wish by whatever means they choose."', 'The final clause of this paragraph directly and explicitly denies the claim in the statement — read to the end of the sentence before answering.', '{"true_false_not_given"}', 60, 7, false),
('reading', 'multiple_choice', 'Urban Planning', 'medium', 6.5, 'What economic concern do some critics raise about restricting car access in certain districts?', '21000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000004', null, '["It could increase local property taxes","It could disproportionately affect tradespeople who rely on vehicles for work","It could reduce funding for public transport","It could raise the price of local housing"]', '"It could disproportionately affect tradespeople who rely on vehicles for work"', 'The passage states restricting car access "could disproportionately affect residents and small business owners who depend on vehicles for their livelihoods, such as tradespeople who transport tools and materials."', 'The example given (tradespeople transporting tools) is the concrete illustration the passage uses — match the option that reflects this specific example.', '{"multiple_choice"}', 65, 8, false),
('reading', 'short_answer', 'Urban Planning', 'medium', 6.5, 'What kind of unrelated online claims have become associated with the fifteen-minute city concept in some cities?', '21000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000004', null, null, '["conspiracy theories","unsubstantiated conspiracy theories"]', 'The passage states the concept "has become entangled in unrelated and largely unsubstantiated conspiracy theories."', 'The phrase "more surprisingly" at the start of that paragraph signals an unexpected turn in the argument, which is a useful place to look for unusual claims like this one.', '{"short_answer"}', 50, 9, false),
('reading', 'true_false_not_given', 'Urban Planning', 'medium', 6.5, 'Comprehensive research evidence already confirms the long-term social and economic effects of fifteen-minute city initiatives.', '21000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000004', null, null, '"FALSE"', 'The passage states "empirical evaluation of fifteen-minute city initiatives remains at an early stage" and that meaningful assessment "will require years of data," contradicting the idea that comprehensive evidence already exists.', 'The final paragraph explicitly cautions against premature conclusions — a claim that evidence is already comprehensive directly contradicts this caution.', '{"true_false_not_given"}', 60, 10, false),
('reading', 'matching_headings', 'Urban Planning', 'medium', 6.5, 'Which paragraph presents the potential benefits argued for by supporters of the concept?', '21000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000004', null, '["Paragraph 1: Introducing the concept","Paragraph 3: Implementation challenges","Paragraph 4: Benefits argued by proponents","Paragraph 5: Criticism regarding inequality and economic effects","Paragraph 7: The need for more evidence"]', '"Paragraph 4: Benefits argued by proponents"', 'Paragraph 4 begins "Proponents argue that the potential benefits extend well beyond convenience," listing environmental, health, and social benefits.', 'Locate the paragraph opening with "Proponents argue" as a direct signal of a benefits-focused paragraph.', '{"matching_headings"}', 70, 11, false),
('reading', 'short_answer', 'Urban Planning', 'medium', 6, 'Name one health-related benefit proponents associate with reduced car dependence, according to the passage.', '21000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000004', null, null, '["higher levels of everyday physical activity","improved local air quality","public health benefits from walking and cycling"]', 'The passage mentions "improved local air quality" and "public health benefits linked to higher levels of everyday physical activity" as benefits of reduced car reliance.', 'Either the air-quality or physical-activity benefit named in paragraph 4 is an acceptable answer here.', '{"short_answer"}', 50, 12, false),
('reading', 'true_false_not_given', 'Urban Planning', 'medium', 6.5, 'The recent global pandemic contributed to renewed public interest in neighbourhood-level amenities.', '21000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000004', null, null, '"TRUE"', 'The passage links the concept''s framing to "widespread experience of local lockdowns during the recent global pandemic, a renewed public appreciation for neighbourhood-level amenities."', 'This detail appears in a long list of contemporary concerns in paragraph 2 — read the whole list rather than stopping at the first item.', '{"true_false_not_given"}', 55, 13, false),
('reading', 'true_false_not_given', 'History', 'medium', 6, 'For most of the twentieth century, the invention of writing was popularly attributed mainly to trade and accounting needs.', '21000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000005', null, null, '"FALSE"', 'The passage states the invention of writing "was popularly explained as an intellectual breakthrough driven primarily by religious or administrative record-keeping needs within temple institutions," not trade and accounting.', 'The passage contrasts the older, popular explanation (religious/temple) with the newer evidence-based one (trade) — do not mix up which explanation belongs to which time period.', '{"true_false_not_given"}', 60, 1, false),
('reading', 'short_answer', 'History', 'medium', 6, 'In roughly which millennium BCE had Sumerian city-states developed extensive trade networks, according to the passage?', '21000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000005', null, null, '["the fourth millennium BCE","fourth millennium BCE"]', 'The passage states "By roughly the fourth millennium BCE, the city-states of ancient Sumer had developed extensive trade networks."', 'Time expressions like "fourth millennium BCE" are precise and easy to scan for once you know roughly which paragraph to check.', '{"short_answer"}', 45, 2, false),
('reading', 'true_false_not_given', 'History', 'hard', 7, 'Clay tokens were used as an accounting system for several millennia before writing developed.', '21000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000005', null, null, '"TRUE"', 'The passage states tokens dating "back to as early as 8000 BCE" predated writing "by several millennia," and "served as a functional... accounting system" over that long period.', 'Combine the earliest date given (8000 BCE) with the later emergence of writing to confirm the span described as "several millennia."', '{"true_false_not_given"}', 65, 3, false),
('reading', 'summary_completion', 'History', 'hard', 7, 'Complete the summary using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS: Tokens representing a transaction were sealed inside a hollow clay container known as a ______, which had to be broken open to verify its contents.', '21000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000005', null, null, '"bulla"', 'The passage states tokens "were sealed together inside a hollow clay ball, or ''bulla,'' which could later be broken open to verify the contents."', 'The term is introduced with quotation marks directly after its description ("hollow clay ball, or..."), a reliable pattern for locating a named object.', '{"summary_completion"}', 60, 4, false),
('reading', 'summary_completion', 'History', 'hard', 7, 'Complete the summary using NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS: Administrators began pressing tokens into the surface of the bulla before sealing them inside, creating a visible ______ of the contents.', '21000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000005', null, null, '"impression"', 'The passage states this process created "a visible impression that recorded the container''s contents without requiring the ball to be broken open."', 'The sentence in the summary closely mirrors the passage''s wording, so identify the exact noun following "creating a visible."', '{"summary_completion"}', 55, 5, false),
('reading', 'multiple_choice', 'History', 'hard', 7, 'What conceptual significance does the passage attach to pressing tokens into the surface of a bulla?', '21000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000005', null, '["It made bullae more durable and less likely to break","It separated the symbolic representation of quantity from the physical tokens themselves","It allowed bullae to be transported more easily over long distances","It reduced the total number of tokens merchants needed to carry"]', '"It separated the symbolic representation of quantity from the physical tokens themselves"', 'The passage states this innovation "separated the symbolic representation of a quantity from the physical tokens themselves," calling it "a conceptual leap of considerable significance."', 'Look for the sentence explicitly describing the innovation''s "conceptual" significance, since the question asks about conceptual rather than practical importance.', '{"multiple_choice"}', 70, 6, false),
('reading', 'true_false_not_given', 'History', 'medium', 6.5, 'The earliest known proto-cuneiform texts are mostly religious or literary in content.', '21000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000005', null, null, '"FALSE"', 'The passage states these early texts "are overwhelmingly administrative and economic in character rather than literary, religious, or historical," directly contradicting the statement.', 'The phrase "rather than" clearly signals what the texts are not — religious or literary — which is exactly what the false statement claims.', '{"true_false_not_given"}', 55, 7, false),
('reading', 'short_answer', 'History', 'medium', 6.5, 'What tool was used to press cuneiform symbols into soft clay tablets?', '21000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000005', null, null, '["a reed stylus","reed stylus"]', 'The passage states cuneiform was "produced by pressing a reed stylus into soft clay tablets."', 'Look near the mention of "wedge-shaped cuneiform writing system" for the specific tool named immediately afterward.', '{"short_answer"}', 45, 8, false),
('reading', 'true_false_not_given', 'History', 'hard', 7, 'Cuneiform eventually developed to represent the sounds of spoken language, not just objects and quantities.', '21000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000005', null, null, '"TRUE"', 'The passage states the script "was eventually adapted to represent not just objects and quantities but the sounds of spoken language itself."', 'This is a close paraphrase of the passage''s own wording — check that both parts of the comparison (objects/quantities vs. sounds) are represented correctly.', '{"true_false_not_given"}', 55, 9, false),
('reading', 'true_false_not_given', 'History', 'hard', 7.5, 'Historians unanimously agree that writing''s later development owed nothing to literary or political ambition.', '21000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000005', null, null, '"FALSE"', 'The passage states some scholars believe "later developments in writing''s expressive range owed as much to literary and political ambition as to accounting necessity," directly contradicting a claim of unanimous agreement that it owed nothing to these factors.', 'A claim of total unanimity ("unanimously agree... owed nothing") should be checked against any dissenting or qualifying viewpoint mentioned near the end of the passage.', '{"true_false_not_given"}', 65, 10, false),
('reading', 'matching_information', 'History', 'medium', 6.5, 'Which paragraph presents a cautionary view against overstating the purely economic origin of writing?', '21000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000005', null, '["Paragraph 2","Paragraph 4","Paragraph 5","Paragraph 6","Paragraph 7"]', '"Paragraph 7"', 'The final paragraph opens with "Some scholars caution against overstating the purely economic origin of writing," matching the question directly.', 'The final paragraph of an academic passage often introduces a qualifying or alternative viewpoint — check there first for "caution" or "however" language.', '{"matching_information"}', 60, 11, false),
('reading', 'multiple_choice', 'History', 'medium', 6.5, 'What did a cone-shaped clay token typically represent, according to the passage?', '21000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000005', null, '["A measure of grain","A quantity of livestock","A unit of textiles","A specific merchant or institution"]', '"A measure of grain"', 'The passage gives the example that "a particular cone shape might represent a measure of grain."', 'The example given for the cone shape is specific and singular in the passage — do not confuse it with the sphere shape mentioned in the same sentence.', '{"multiple_choice"}', 55, 12, false),
('reading', 'short_answer', 'History', 'medium', 6.5, 'What name do scholars give to the early pictographic script that emerged from the token and bulla system?', '21000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000005', null, null, '["proto-cuneiform"]', 'The passage states this transition marks "the emergence of what scholars now call proto-cuneiform, an early pictographic script."', 'The phrase "what scholars now call" is a direct signal that a defined term follows immediately.', '{"short_answer"}', 50, 13, false),
('reading', 'short_answer', 'Biology', 'medium', 6, 'What term does the passage use for the scientific field studying medicinal-like behaviours in animals?', '21000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000006', null, null, '["zoopharmacognosy"]', 'The passage states this field of study "is now generally referred to as zoopharmacognosy."', 'This unusual technical term is defined immediately in the first paragraph — note its component meanings given in the passage to help you spell and recall it.', '{"short_answer"}', 45, 1, false),
('reading', 'true_false_not_given', 'Biology', 'medium', 6, 'Chimpanzees observed chewing bitter plant pith used a preparation method similar to one used by some local human populations.', '21000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000006', null, null, '"TRUE"', 'The passage describes the chimpanzees'' preparation method as "notably similar to that used by some local human populations for the same plant to treat intestinal complaints."', 'The comparison between chimpanzee and human preparation methods is stated explicitly in a single sentence — locate it directly.', '{"true_false_not_given"}', 55, 2, false),
('reading', 'true_false_not_given', 'Biology', 'hard', 7, 'Laboratory analysis found that the plant chewed by chimpanzees had no measurable effect against intestinal parasites.', '21000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000006', null, null, '"FALSE"', 'The passage states laboratory analysis "confirmed that the plant contains compounds with demonstrated activity against intestinal parasites," directly contradicting the statement of no effect.', 'The word "confirmed" plus "demonstrated activity" strongly signals a positive finding, the opposite of "no measurable effect" in the question.', '{"true_false_not_given"}', 55, 3, false),
('reading', 'multiple_choice', 'Biology', 'medium', 6.5, 'What is the proposed function of whole-leaf swallowing behaviour in great apes, according to the passage?', '21000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000006', null, '["It provides essential nutrients otherwise missing from their diet","It mechanically dislodges and expels intestinal parasites","It signals social status within the group","It helps regulate body temperature"]', '"It mechanically dislodges and expels intestinal parasites"', 'The passage states researchers propose "the physical texture of these leaves helps to mechanically dislodge and expel intestinal parasites as they pass through the gut."', 'The mechanism described (rough texture, mechanical dislodging) is distinct from the chemical mechanism in the pith-chewing example — do not conflate the two.', '{"multiple_choice"}', 65, 4, false),
('reading', 'true_false_not_given', 'Biology', 'medium', 6.5, 'Leaf-swallowing behaviour occurs at a constant rate throughout the year regardless of parasite levels.', '21000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000006', null, null, '"FALSE"', 'The passage states the behaviour "occurs disproportionately during periods and seasons associated with elevated parasite loads," meaning it is not constant throughout the year.', '"Disproportionately during" certain seasons directly rules out a claim of constant, unvarying occurrence.', '{"true_false_not_given"}', 55, 5, false),
('reading', 'matching_features', 'Biology', 'hard', 7, 'Match each self-medicating behaviour to the species that performs it: Applies plant resins with antimicrobial properties to the colony''s nest structure.', '21000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000006', null, '["Chimpanzees","Ants","Birds","Butterflies"]', '"Ants"', 'The passage states certain ant species "have been observed to seek out and apply plant resins with antimicrobial properties to the nest structure itself."', 'Each species example in this paragraph is introduced by name early in its sentence — scan for the species name first, then confirm the matching behaviour.', '{"matching_features"}', 60, 6, false),
('reading', 'matching_features', 'Biology', 'hard', 7, 'Match each self-medicating behaviour to the species that performs it: Lines its nest with aromatic plants shown to repel parasitic mites.', '21000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000006', null, '["Chimpanzees","Ants","Birds","Butterflies"]', '"Birds"', 'The passage states "some birds line their nests with specific aromatic plants shown in laboratory testing to repel parasitic mites."', 'The word "nests" combined with "mites" is a distinctive pairing that appears only in the sentence about birds.', '{"matching_features"}', 55, 7, false),
('reading', 'matching_features', 'Biology', 'hard', 7, 'Match each self-medicating behaviour to the species that performs it: Selects host plants for its eggs based on chemical compounds that will later protect its offspring.', '21000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000006', null, '["Chimpanzees","Ants","Birds","Butterflies"]', '"Butterflies"', 'The passage states certain butterfly species "select host plants for their eggs based partly on the plant''s chemical profile, effectively provisioning their future offspring with compounds that will later confer some protection."', 'This is the only example describing medication for offspring rather than for the individual performing the behaviour, which makes it easy to distinguish.', '{"matching_features"}', 60, 8, false),
('reading', 'true_false_not_given', 'Biology', 'hard', 7, 'Most researchers believe that invertebrate self-medicating behaviours require conscious understanding of cause and effect.', '21000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000006', null, null, '"FALSE"', 'The passage states researchers argue such a behaviour "could become genetically fixed within a population... without requiring any cognitive understanding of cause and effect on the part of the individual animals performing it," and that most favour "a largely instinctive explanation."', 'The phrase "without requiring any cognitive understanding" is a direct negation of the claim in the question.', '{"true_false_not_given"}', 60, 9, false),
('reading', 'multiple_choice', 'Biology', 'hard', 7, 'What evidence has led some researchers to argue for a form of "cultural" transmission in some primate self-medicating behaviours?', '21000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000006', null, '["The behaviour appears identically in every individual within a group at the same time","The behaviour spreads in a pattern consistent with younger individuals observing and learning from others","The behaviour has been observed only in captivity, never in the wild","The behaviour disappears entirely once a group is well-fed"]', '"The behaviour spreads in a pattern consistent with younger individuals observing and learning from others"', 'The passage notes the behaviour "is sometimes observed to spread through a group in a pattern consistent with social learning, in which younger or less experienced individuals appear to acquire the behaviour partly by observing others."', 'Eliminate the option claiming uniform, simultaneous behaviour across all individuals, since the passage explicitly says "not all individuals... engage in a given... behaviour at any one time."', '{"multiple_choice"}', 75, 10, false),
('reading', 'true_false_not_given', 'Biology', 'hard', 7.5, 'The idea of social learning in animal self-medication is universally accepted among researchers in the field.', '21000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000006', null, null, '"FALSE"', 'The passage states this interpretation "remains genuinely contested within the field," and that demonstrating social learning conclusively "remains notoriously difficult," contradicting universal acceptance.', 'The word "contested" is a strong, unambiguous signal against any claim of universal agreement.', '{"true_false_not_given"}', 60, 11, false),
('reading', 'summary_completion', 'Biology', 'medium', 6.5, 'Complete the summary using NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS: Some pharmaceutical researchers use an informal strategy sometimes called "______" to identify potentially useful compounds by studying substances animals select for apparent medicinal purposes.', '21000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000006', null, null, '"following the animals"', 'The passage names this strategy "sometimes informally described as ''following the animals'' to shortcut the traditionally slow process of screening plant compounds."', 'The phrase is placed in quotation marks in the final paragraph, making it easy to identify once you reach that section.', '{"summary_completion"}', 60, 12, false),
('reading', 'short_answer', 'Biology', 'medium', 6.5, 'According to the final paragraph, what is the "following the animals" research strategy compared with in terms of its current prominence?', '21000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000006', null, null, '["a relatively minor strand within pharmaceutical research","more conventional screening methods"]', 'The passage states this approach "remains a relatively minor strand within pharmaceutical research compared with more conventional screening methods."', 'The word "compared with" directly introduces the second half of the comparison the question is asking about.', '{"short_answer"}', 55, 13, false),
('reading', 'note_completion', 'Leisure', 'easy', 4.5, 'Complete the note using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS: The swimming pool closes ______ before the rest of the centre closes.', '22000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001', null, null, '"thirty minutes"', 'The Opening Hours section states "The swimming pool closes thirty minutes before the rest of the centre to allow time for cleaning."', 'Scan the Opening Hours heading first, since the answer to a timing question is almost always located directly under a matching heading.', '{"note_completion"}', 45, 1, false),
('reading', 'form_completion', 'Leisure', 'easy', 4.5, 'Complete the form using NO MORE THAN ONE WORD OR A NUMBER: Guest fee per visit: £______', '22000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001', null, null, '"8"', 'The Guest Policy section states "Guests are charged a flat fee of £8 per visit, payable at reception."', 'When a blank is preceded by a currency symbol, you only need to supply the number, not the symbol itself.', '{"form_completion"}', 40, 2, false),
('reading', 'table_completion', 'Leisure', 'medium', 5.5, 'Complete the table using NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS: Membership: Gold | Monthly price: £59 | Extra included: two free ______ sessions per month', '22000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001', null, null, '"personal training"', 'The Membership Types section states the Gold membership "includes everything in Silver plus two free personal training sessions each month."', 'In a table with several membership tiers, locate the tier name first, then read only the sentence describing that tier to avoid mixing up details from Bronze or Silver.', '{"table_completion"}', 55, 3, false),
('reading', 'multiple_choice', 'Leisure', 'medium', 5.5, 'What is stated about a seven-year-old child visiting the centre?', '22000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001', null, '["They may use the gymnasium unaccompanied","They may use the swimming pool if accompanied by an adult member","They may not use the swimming pool under any circumstances","They need no adult supervision in the group exercise studio"]', '"They may not use the swimming pool under any circumstances"', 'The passage states children "aged eight and above may use the swimming pool if accompanied by a paying adult member," which implies a seven-year-old, being under eight, may not use the pool at all.', 'When a rule gives a minimum age for permission, treat anyone below that age as excluded, even if the passage does not say so in a separate sentence.', '{"multiple_choice"}', 70, 4, false),
