('reading', 'multiple_choice', 'Workplace', 'hard', 6.5, 'According to the handbook, when might an employee be allowed to carry over more than the standard leave carry-over limit?', '22000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002', null, '["If they are a part-time employee","If they used the online scheduling system correctly","If they could not take the leave due to approved sick, maternity, or paternity leave","If they are a departmental head"]', '"If they could not take the leave due to approved sick, maternity, or paternity leave"', 'The passage states leave beyond the five-day limit "is forfeited unless the employee was unable to take it due to approved sick leave or maternity or paternity leave," meaning this is the only stated exception.', 'Look for the word "unless" — it introduces the one exception to the general rule stated just before it.', '{"multiple_choice"}', 70, 6, false),
('reading', 'sentence_completion', 'Workplace', 'easy', 5, 'Complete the sentence using NO MORE THAN ONE WORD: Employees who are ill must notify their line manager by ______ before their scheduled start time.', '22000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002', null, null, '"telephone"', 'The passage states employees "must notify their line manager by telephone before their scheduled start time, rather than by text message or email."', 'When a sentence lists an accepted method followed by rejected alternatives ("rather than"), the blank refers to the accepted one only.', '{"sentence_completion"}', 45, 7, false),
