('reading', 'matching_headings', 'Society', 'hard', 6.5, 'Choose the correct heading for Paragraph 2 from the list below: i. Early predictions of handwriting''s disappearance / ii. Renewed enthusiasm for handwriting outside educational settings / iii. Research comparing note-taking methods / iv. A neurological explanation for handwriting''s advantages / v. Disagreement over school curriculum decisions / vi. Concerns about equity and accessibility / vii. A hybrid approach for the future / viii. The financial cost of handwriting instruction', '22000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000003', null, '["Early predictions of handwriting''s disappearance","Renewed enthusiasm for handwriting outside educational settings","Research comparing note-taking methods","A neurological explanation for handwriting''s advantages","Disagreement over school curriculum decisions","Concerns about equity and accessibility","A hybrid approach for the future","The financial cost of handwriting instruction"]', '"Research comparing note-taking methods"', 'Paragraph 2 describes studies comparing "note-taking on laptops with note-taking by hand" and the resulting "generation effect," matching this heading exactly.', 'Identify the paragraph''s main subject in your own words first, then match it to the heading — do not simply pick the heading with the most repeated words.', '{"matching_headings"}', 75, 1, false),
('reading', 'matching_headings', 'Society', 'hard', 6.5, 'Choose the correct heading for Paragraph 3 from the list below: i. Early predictions of handwriting''s disappearance / ii. Renewed enthusiasm for handwriting outside educational settings / iii. Research comparing note-taking methods / iv. A neurological explanation for handwriting''s advantages / v. Disagreement over school curriculum decisions / vi. Concerns about equity and accessibility / vii. A hybrid approach for the future / viii. The financial cost of handwriting instruction', '22000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000003', null, '["Early predictions of handwriting''s disappearance","Renewed enthusiasm for handwriting outside educational settings","Research comparing note-taking methods","A neurological explanation for handwriting''s advantages","Disagreement over school curriculum decisions","Concerns about equity and accessibility","A hybrid approach for the future","The financial cost of handwriting instruction"]', '"A neurological explanation for handwriting''s advantages"', 'Paragraph 3 discusses brain imaging research showing handwriting "activates a broader and more interconnected network of brain regions than typing," which is a neurological explanation.', 'The presence of scientific terms like "brain imaging" and "neurological basis" is a strong clue pointing toward a heading about brain science.', '{"matching_headings"}', 75, 2, false),
('reading', 'matching_headings', 'Society', 'hard', 7, 'Choose the correct heading for Paragraph 4 from the list below: i. Early predictions of handwriting''s disappearance / ii. Renewed enthusiasm for handwriting outside educational settings / iii. Research comparing note-taking methods / iv. A neurological explanation for handwriting''s advantages / v. Disagreement over school curriculum decisions / vi. Concerns about equity and accessibility / vii. A hybrid approach for the future / viii. The financial cost of handwriting instruction', '22000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000003', null, '["Early predictions of handwriting''s disappearance","Renewed enthusiasm for handwriting outside educational settings","Research comparing note-taking methods","A neurological explanation for handwriting''s advantages","Disagreement over school curriculum decisions","Concerns about equity and accessibility","A hybrid approach for the future","The financial cost of handwriting instruction"]', '"Disagreement over school curriculum decisions"', 'Paragraph 4 presents both the reinstatement of cursive by some school systems and critics who "argue that reinstating cursive risks displacing instructional time," showing clear disagreement about curriculum policy.', 'When a paragraph presents two opposing viewpoints, look for a heading that signals disagreement or debate rather than one describing only a single position.', '{"matching_headings"}', 80, 3, false),
('reading', 'matching_headings', 'Society', 'hard', 7, 'Choose the correct heading for Paragraph 6 from the list below: i. Early predictions of handwriting''s disappearance / ii. Renewed enthusiasm for handwriting outside educational settings / iii. Research comparing note-taking methods / iv. A neurological explanation for handwriting''s advantages / v. Disagreement over school curriculum decisions / vi. Concerns about equity and accessibility / vii. A hybrid approach for the future / viii. The financial cost of handwriting instruction', '22000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000003', null, '["Early predictions of handwriting''s disappearance","Renewed enthusiasm for handwriting outside educational settings","Research comparing note-taking methods","A neurological explanation for handwriting''s advantages","Disagreement over school curriculum decisions","Concerns about equity and accessibility","A hybrid approach for the future","The financial cost of handwriting instruction"]', '"Concerns about equity and accessibility"', 'Paragraph 6 warns that for people "with dysgraphia, motor impairments, or certain learning differences, handwriting is not a superior option but a genuine barrier," which is a concern about equity and accessibility.', 'Terms like "barrier," "disadvantaging," and "accessible" in a paragraph are strong indicators of a heading about equity or accessibility.', '{"matching_headings"}', 80, 4, false),
('reading', 'true_false_not_given', 'Society', 'medium', 6, 'The studies comparing note-taking methods found that laptop users wrote fewer words than pen-and-paper users.', '22000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000003', null, null, '"FALSE"', 'The passage states typists "typically recorded more words overall" than students taking notes by hand, which is the opposite of the statement.', 'Watch for a comparison being reversed — the statement swaps which group wrote more, so check the direction of the comparison carefully.', '{"true_false_not_given"}', 55, 5, false),
('reading', 'true_false_not_given', 'Society', 'medium', 6, 'The "generation effect" refers to information that must be actively reformulated being more likely to be remembered.', '22000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000003', null, null, '"TRUE"', 'The passage directly defines the term: "information that must be actively reformulated, rather than merely copied, is more likely to be encoded in long-term memory."', 'When a technical term is introduced in quotation marks, its definition almost always follows immediately in the same or next clause.', '{"true_false_not_given"}', 55, 6, false),
('reading', 'true_false_not_given', 'Society', 'hard', 7, 'Brain imaging research has definitively proven that handwriting causes better memory than typing.', '22000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000003', null, null, '"FALSE"', 'The passage says researchers "cannot fully rule out other explanations," which directly contradicts the claim that the link has been "definitively proven."', 'Absolute claims like "definitively proven" should be checked against any hedging language nearby, such as "cannot fully rule out."', '{"true_false_not_given"}', 65, 7, false),
('reading', 'short_answer', 'Society', 'medium', 6, 'What kind of movement does typing involve, according to the passage, regardless of which letter is pressed?', '22000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000003', null, null, '["the same small, repetitive motion","small, repetitive motion"]', 'The passage states typing "involves the same small, repetitive motion regardless of which letter is pressed."', 'Look for the contrast word "whereas" in the sentence about letter formation — the second half of that sentence answers this question.', '{"short_answer"}', 55, 8, false),
('reading', 'multiple_choice', 'Society', 'medium', 6, 'Why have some school systems reinstated cursive handwriting instruction?', '22000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000003', null, '["To reduce the amount of time students spend using computers","Because students without cursive skills struggle to read historical documents and handwritten letters","Because international exams now require cursive answers","Because typing proficiency is no longer considered a necessary skill"]', '"Because students without cursive skills struggle to read historical documents and handwritten letters"', 'The passage states schools reinstated cursive citing "students who are never taught cursive struggle to read historical documents, handwritten family letters, and even... cursive signatures."', 'Eliminate options not mentioned anywhere in the passage, such as exam requirements or reduced screen time, which are never discussed.', '{"multiple_choice"}', 70, 9, false),
('reading', 'summary_completion', 'Society', 'hard', 6.5, 'Complete the summary using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS: Sales of notebooks have grown even among ______ consumers, partly owing to structured systems such as bullet journaling.', '22000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000003', null, null, '"digitally native"', 'The passage states notebook sales have grown "even among younger, digitally native consumers, a trend widely attributed to the popularity of bullet journaling."', 'Match the summary sentence structure closely to the original sentence to locate the missing adjective describing the consumers.', '{"summary_completion"}', 60, 10, false),
('reading', 'summary_completion', 'Society', 'hard', 6.5, 'Complete the summary using NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS: Advocates say the slower pace of handwriting offers relief from ______, a form of mental tiredness caused by extended screen-based work.', '22000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000003', null, null, '"digital fatigue"', 'The passage defines "digital fatigue" as "the sense of mental depletion that can follow long stretches of screen-based work and communication."', 'The summary paraphrases the passage''s own definition, so match "mental tiredness" in the question to "mental depletion" in the text.', '{"summary_completion"}', 60, 11, false),
('reading', 'summary_completion', 'Society', 'hard', 6.5, 'Complete the summary using NO MORE THAN ONE WORD: Critics warn that treating handwriting as superior could disadvantage students with ______ or motor impairments.', '22000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000003', null, null, '"dysgraphia"', 'The passage states handwriting "is not a superior option but a genuine barrier" for individuals "with dysgraphia, motor impairments, or certain learning differences."', 'Since the second condition ("motor impairments") is already given in the summary, search the sentence in the passage that lists it alongside the missing word.', '{"summary_completion"}', 55, 12, false),
('reading', 'short_answer', 'Society', 'medium', 6, 'What feature do several major note-taking application developers now offer that converts handwritten notes into searchable digital text?', '22000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000003', null, null, '["stylus-based handwriting recognition","handwriting recognition features"]', 'The final paragraph states developers have "introduced stylus-based handwriting recognition features that convert handwritten notes into searchable digital text."', 'The answer sits in the same sentence as the phrase used in the question ("converts handwritten notes into searchable digital text") — locate that phrase and read backward.', '{"short_answer"}', 55, 13, false),
('reading', 'true_false_not_given', 'Society', 'medium', 6, 'Most researchers now recommend that people abandon typing altogether in favour of handwriting.', '22000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000003', null, null, '"FALSE"', 'The passage states "most researchers in the field stop well short of recommending a wholesale return to handwriting," directly contradicting the claim.', 'The phrase "stop well short of recommending" is a strong negation — do not be misled by the earlier discussion of handwriting''s benefits.', '{"true_false_not_given"}', 55, 14, false),
