('reading', 'matching_headings', 'Science', 'hard', 6.5, 'Choose the correct heading for Paragraph 2 from the list below: i. Cultural differences in reporting déjà vu across countries / ii. Long-standing mystical explanations for the experience / iii. Familiarity created by overlapping features of a scene / iv. Clinical evidence from epilepsy patients / v. A memory framework distinguishing two recognition processes / vi. Why the sensation becomes less frequent with age / vii. New laboratory methods for triggering the sensation / viii. Wider implications for understanding memory disorders', '22000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000006', null, '["Cultural differences in reporting déjà vu across countries","Long-standing mystical explanations for the experience","Familiarity created by overlapping features of a scene","Clinical evidence from epilepsy patients","A memory framework distinguishing two recognition processes","Why the sensation becomes less frequent with age","New laboratory methods for triggering the sensation","Wider implications for understanding memory disorders"]', '"Familiarity created by overlapping features of a scene"', 'Paragraph 2 explains that a new environment sharing "enough incidental features with a genuinely forgotten past experience" can trigger a false sense of familiarity.', 'Look for the specific mechanism described (overlapping features of a scene) rather than the general topic (déjà vu), since several headings relate to déjà vu broadly.', '{"matching_headings"}', 80, 1, false),
