('reading', 'matching_headings', 'Science', 'hard', 7, 'Choose the correct heading for Paragraph 4 from the list below: i. Cultural differences in reporting déjà vu across countries / ii. Long-standing mystical explanations for the experience / iii. Familiarity created by overlapping features of a scene / iv. Clinical evidence from epilepsy patients / v. A memory framework distinguishing two recognition processes / vi. Why the sensation becomes less frequent with age / vii. New laboratory methods for triggering the sensation / viii. Wider implications for understanding memory disorders', '22000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000006', null, '["Cultural differences in reporting déjà vu across countries","Long-standing mystical explanations for the experience","Familiarity created by overlapping features of a scene","Clinical evidence from epilepsy patients","A memory framework distinguishing two recognition processes","Why the sensation becomes less frequent with age","New laboratory methods for triggering the sensation","Wider implications for understanding memory disorders"]', '"A memory framework distinguishing two recognition processes"', 'Paragraph 4 introduces "the dual-process model, which distinguishes between two separate cognitive operations... familiarity... and recollection."', 'The number "two" appearing prominently in a paragraph about a named model is a strong clue for headings mentioning a distinction between processes.', '{"matching_headings"}', 80, 3, false),
('reading', 'matching_headings', 'Science', 'hard', 7, 'Choose the correct heading for Paragraph 6 from the list below: i. Cultural differences in reporting déjà vu across countries / ii. Long-standing mystical explanations for the experience / iii. Familiarity created by overlapping features of a scene / iv. Clinical evidence from epilepsy patients / v. A memory framework distinguishing two recognition processes / vi. Why the sensation becomes less frequent with age / vii. New laboratory methods for triggering the sensation / viii. Wider implications for understanding memory disorders', '22000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000006', null, '["Cultural differences in reporting déjà vu across countries","Long-standing mystical explanations for the experience","Familiarity created by overlapping features of a scene","Clinical evidence from epilepsy patients","A memory framework distinguishing two recognition processes","Why the sensation becomes less frequent with age","New laboratory methods for triggering the sensation","Wider implications for understanding memory disorders"]', '"New laboratory methods for triggering the sensation"', 'Paragraph 6 describes "the development of laboratory methods capable of reliably inducing a déjà-vu-like state under controlled conditions," matching this heading directly.', 'Words like "laboratory," "induced," and "controlled conditions" are strong signals of a heading about experimental methods.', '{"matching_headings"}', 75, 4, false),
('reading', 'true_false_not_given', 'Science', 'medium', 6, 'Surveys suggest that more than half of people experience déjà vu at least once in their lives.', '22000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000006', null, null, '"TRUE"', 'The passage states "survey estimates suggest that between sixty and seventy per cent of people experience it at least once in their lives," which is more than half.', 'Convert the given percentage range into a simple fraction (over 50%) to check it against the statement quickly.', '{"true_false_not_given"}', 50, 5, false),
