('listening', 'note_completion', 'Academic lecture', 'medium', 6.5, 'Before an eruption, volcanoes release increasing amounts of ______ gas.', null, '33000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000004', null, '"sulphur dioxide"', 'The lecturer says volcanoes "typically release increasing amounts of sulphur dioxide gas."', 'Chemical names are frequently tested — practise recognising "sulphur dioxide" by ear as it is easy to confuse with similar terms.', '{"note_completion"}', 45, 5, false),
('listening', 'multiple_choice', 'Academic lecture', 'hard', 7, 'Why do scientists generally avoid giving precise eruption predictions?', null, '33000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000004', '["Because seismometers are too expensive to install widely","Because volcanoes showing warning signs may not erupt for months or years","Because governments do not allow public warnings","Because gas monitoring equipment is unreliable"]', '"Because volcanoes showing warning signs may not erupt for months or years"', 'The lecturer explains that "some volcanoes show all the warning signs and then don''t erupt for months, or even years," which is why precise predictions are avoided.', 'For "why" questions in a lecture, listen for the reasoning clause immediately before or after the word "because" or "since."', '{"multiple_choice"}', 55, 6, false),
('listening', 'note_completion', 'Academic lecture', 'hard', 7, 'Instead of exact predictions, scientists issue a colour-coded ______ level.', null, '33000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000004', null, '["hazard alert","hazard alert level"]', 'The lecturer says scientists "issue what''s called a hazard alert level, usually on a colour-coded scale."', 'Terms defined with "what''s called" are a strong signal of an exact-answer gap-fill.', '{"note_completion"}', 45, 7, false),
('listening', 'form_completion', 'Academic lecture', 'hard', 7.5, 'Before its 1980 eruption, Mount St Helens'' north face bulged at around ______ metres per day.', null, '33000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000004', null, '["1.5","one and a half"]', 'The lecturer says the bulge grew "at a rate of around one and a half metres per day in the weeks before the eruption."', 'Fractional numbers ("one and a half") should usually be written as a decimal (1.5) unless told otherwise.', '{"form_completion"}', 50, 8, false),
('listening', 'short_answer', 'Academic lecture', 'hard', 7.5, 'What three types of data are combined in modern eruption-forecasting models?', null, '33000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000004', null, '["seismic, deformation, and gas measurements","seismic, deformation and gas"]', 'The lecturer says researchers are "combining multiple types of data — seismic, deformation, and gas measurements."', 'When a lecture recaps several earlier points in one list near the end, match each item back to what was explained in detail earlier.', '{"short_answer"}', 50, 9, false),
('listening', 'multiple_choice', 'Academic lecture', 'hard', 8, 'What do researchers say about the multi-parameter approach, according to the lecture''s conclusion?', null, '33000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000004', '["It guarantees an exact eruption date","It improves forecasting accuracy but cannot guarantee an exact date","It has not improved forecasting at all","It only works for Mount St Helens"]', '"It improves forecasting accuracy but cannot guarantee an exact date"', 'The lecture concludes that the approach "improves forecasting accuracy considerably...although scientists are always careful to stress that no method can currently guarantee an exact eruption date."', 'Concluding sentences with "although" often contain a balanced view — make sure your chosen option reflects both halves of the statement, not just one.', '{"multiple_choice"}', 55, 10, false);

